{
  "$comment": "Retired-model state. Applies to official BYOK providers; relay connections keep relay/model-selection.v1.json (removed banner). Catalog shape per provider: models[] (id, displayName, lifecycle?), retiredModels[] (tombstones {id, displayName, retiredAt, routedTo}), resolveMap, defaultModelId. userModels = the connection's enabled model ids (custom ids included). Conversation status for modelId M, first match wins: (1) catalog null (not loaded) -> available; (2) M in retiredModels -> retired, successorId = routedTo when routedTo is an id in models[] that is itself available at `now`, else null; (3) M in models[] with lifecycle.state deprecated and shutdownAt <= now -> retired, successorId = lifecycle.routedTo under the same rule, else null; (4) M in models[] -> available; (5) M in userModels -> available (hand-entered id); (6) resolveMap[M] is in models[] -> available (canonical alias); (7) else missing, successorId null. retired and missing both show banner.model_retired and block sending; available never does. The conversation modelId is never rewritten and nothing is synced outward until the user acts (modelIdAfter == modelId in every case). Display name, first non-empty wins: storedName -> models[] displayName for M -> tombstone displayName -> M. newChatCases (no conversation yet): preferredModelId (last used / user default) if available and in userModels; else the enabled model that the metadata defaultModelId matches (iOS ModelResolver.matchingModel, among userModels that are available; return the enabled id, not the catalog id): tier 1 exact — query candidates in order [id, id without the end's own manual-model prefix, id without date suffix, both], case-insensitive, compared to the enabled id; tier 2 alias — first enabled model (list order) whose canonical id (userModelCanonicalIds, else its id), its id, its id without date suffix or its canonical without date suffix equals any candidate; date suffix = -YYYYMMDD or -YYYY-MM-DD at the end only (-MMDD, -latest, @date are not dates); no prefix or substring matching; an enabled model whose own id is retired (tombstone, or deprecated past shutdownAt) is skipped even when its canonical id is available — the canonical is consulted only when its own id is missing from the catalog; relay connections are out of scope here (literal id, relay/model-selection.v1.json); else first id of userModels that is available; hint = last_used_retired exactly when preferredModelId was non-null and not used (shown once per device per provider+model). Test names: RETIRED-<id> (iOS/Android function names contain RETIRED_<id>).",
